guamp: GPU-written imports (IOSurface render targets) cleaned and invalidated by physical address before/after a client's jobs while armed (black app switcher previews)

fin36 and fin55 (live-20261106-092610): the app switcher shows black or old previews. The board maps GPU-written imports clean once and
leaves them alone afterwards (native_adreno_written_imports_owned: about 60 ms a frame otherwise), so the only cache maintenance of a
surface the GPU wrote was the bridge's (adreno-metal 0001/0010: DC CIVAC by virtual address in the writing process, first 4 writes,
again after 500 ms of rest). When the app closes SpringBoard no longer maps the snapshot's pages: DC by VA faulted (SIGSEGV, fin55),
0060 now skips those pages, and the CPU's stale or dirty lines stay over the pixels the GPU wrote (black preview).
NativeAdrenoVm::maintainWritten walks the window's GPU-written imports by physical address (NativeAdrenoMemory::maintainImported,
whoever maps the pages) after each client job (release(), which wait() runs before the waiter returns) and, with bit 1, before it.
Jobs name only their IBs, so the kernel does not know which surface a job wrote: as 0001/0010 per surface, a mapping is walked at the
first N completed jobs of its window after map or after the window rested (NativeAdrenoWrittenPlan.h). The render server's window is
left out by default (its frame buffers are rewritten every frame and read by the display copy, which maintains them itself).
Board switches (GuampAdrenoProbe.cpp): guamp-adreno-written-clean (default 1: after the job; 3: before too; 0: off, as before),
-n (default 4; 0 every job), -gap-ms (default 500), -rs (default 0), -max-mib (a pass's cap, default 32). Counters:
native_adreno_written_stats, logged every 10 s by GuampGpuDcvs.inc ("GuampGpu: written imports by PA: ...").
Host test: drivers/GuampAdreno/tests/written_host.cpp (run-tests.sh).

